"Vertex $({{h}},{{k}})$ gives $f(x)=a(x {{nh|term}})^2 {{k|term}}$.","Substitute $({{x1}},{{y1}})$: ${{y1}}=a({{x1}} {{nh|term}})^2 {{k|term}}=a\\cdot {{dx2}} {{k|term}}$, so $a=\\frac{{{ady}}}{{{dx2}}}={{a}}$.","So the function is $f(x)={{a|coef}}(x {{nh|term}})^2 {{k|term}}$."],"commonError":"Writing the bracket as $(x {{h|term}})$: vertex form uses $x-h$, so the vertex coordinate {{h}} appears with the opposite sign.","answerSummary":"$f(x)={{a|coef}}(x {{nh|term}})^2 {{k|term}}$"},"assessmentItemFormat":"multipleChoice","choices":[{"id":"choice-b","label":"$f(x)={{a|coef}}(x {{nh|term}})^2 {{k|term}}$"},{"id":"choice-c","label":"$f(x)={{a|coef}}(x {{h|term}})^2 {{k|term}}$"},{"id":"choice-d","label":"$f(x)={{aneg|coef}}(x {{nh|term}})^2 {{k|term}}$"},{"id":"choice-a","label":"$f(x)={{a|coef}}(x {{nh1|term}})^2 {{k1|term}}$"}],"responseFields":[{"id":"answer","label":"Choose the correct answer","inputProfile":"choice","expected":"choice-b"}]},{"id":"mm_sat_A_6B_standard-coefficient-from-vertex_v21","active":true,"alignmentKeys":["texas:A.6B"],"alignments":[{"framework":"teks","code":"A.6B","role":"primary","evidenceLevel":"assessed"},{"framework":"digitalSAT","domainId":"advancedMath","role":"primary","evidenceMode":"direct"}],"assessmentContext":{"framework":"digitalSAT","examStyle":true,"domainId":"advancedMath"},"courseId":"algebra1","familyId":"mathmaster:sat:A.6B:standard-coefficient-from-vertex","familyVersion":2,"questionType":"response","activityRole":"practice","difficultyBand":3,"dok":2,"calculatorPolicy":"graphing","assessedConstruct":"A.6B","taskType":"equivalentRepresentation","representation":"vertexToStandard","ccmrChallengeTier":1,"ccmrFamilyRole":"direct","ccmrAuthenticLanguage":{"version":"2.1","authored":true,"officialSkillFamily":"nonlinear functions","stemProfile":"standard-coefficient-from-vertex"},"prompt":"The function $f(x)={{a}}(x {{nh|signed}})^2 {{k|signed}}$ can be written as $f(x)={{a}}x^2+bx+c$. What is the value of $b$?","generator